SYSTEM git: the operations pk runs
REPORTS git's message
RUNS
    fetch tags
    fetch the branch
    commit
    reset to the commit before
    switch
    fast-forward
    tag
    push the branch and the tag
    push the branch

PLACE working tree ONE LASTING
    SAYS What is checked out. git replaces it whole; a definition above can name the files in it.
PLACE tags MANY LASTING
PLACE remote-tracking branch ONE LASTING
PLACE the branch SERIES LASTING GIVEN
PLACE the other branch SERIES LASTING GIVEN
PLACE origin LASTING
PLACE origin's tags MANY LASTING IN origin
PLACE origin's branch SERIES LASTING IN origin GIVEN
PLACE git's message ONE REPORT

FAULT origin does not answer ABOUT origin
    SAYS the remote cannot be reached, or does not have what is asked for
FAULT the commit cannot be made
    SAYS git commit exits non-zero
FAULT the branch cannot be fast-forwarded
    SAYS the other branch's history does not contain the branch's last commit
FAULT the tag cannot be created
    SAYS git tag exits non-zero for a reason other than the name being taken
FAULT origin rejects the push
    SAYS a ref is not a fast-forward of origin's, or origin refuses it for a reason of its own
FAULT the switch fails
    SAYS git switch exits non-zero for a reason other than local changes
OPEN a merge refuses a tree with changes it would overwrite
    SAYS git merge --ff-only stops when the working tree has uncommitted changes to files the merge changes. The part of the manual read does not say.
FACT origin's tag names the commit pushed ONLY origin's tags already has the member
    SAYS origin already has the tag, on the commit the push sends

ACTION fetch tags
    READS origin's tags
    CREATE tags MANY FROM origin's tags
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
    FAIL WHEN tags already has the member
        SAYS The update is rejected, the other tags are created, and git exits 1.
    ACCEPT WHEN tags is given a key twice
        BECAUSE A remote holds one tag of each name.
    SAYS git fetch origin --tags. An update to a tag that exists locally is rejected without --force; git 2.54 then exits 1, and still creates the other tags.

ACTION fetch the branch
    READS origin's branch
    REPLACE remote-tracking branch FROM origin's branch
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
    ACCEPT WHEN remote-tracking branch holds what is kept nowhere
        BECAUSE A remote-tracking branch is a copy of origin's branch, and a fetch makes it again.
    SAYS git fetch origin <branch>.

ACTION commit
    READS working tree
    CREATE the branch FROM working tree
    REFUSE WHEN the commit cannot be made
    SAYS git commit: the working tree's changes become a new commit on the branch.

ACTION reset to the commit before
    READS the branch
    DESTROY the branch
    REPLACE working tree FROM the branch
    ACCEPT WHEN the branch is held elsewhere
        BECAUSE reset moves the branch as asked. It does not look for other holders of the commit.
    ACCEPT WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
        BECAUSE --hard overwrites all files with the version from the commit.
    SAYS git reset --hard HEAD~1. The manual: overwrite all files and directories with the version from the commit.

ACTION switch
    READS the branch
    REPLACE working tree FROM the branch
    REFUSE WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
    REFUSE WHEN the switch fails
    SAYS git switch <branch>. The manual: the operation is aborted if it leads to loss of local changes.

ACTION fast-forward
    READS
        the branch
        the other branch
    CREATE the branch FROM the other branch
    REPLACE working tree FROM the branch
    REFUSE WHEN the branch cannot be fast-forwarded
    REFUSE WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere AND a merge refuses a tree with changes it would overwrite
    SAYS git merge --ff-only <other>. The manual: when not possible, refuse to merge and exit with a non-zero status.

ACTION tag
    READS the branch
    CREATE tags FROM the branch
    REFUSE WHEN tags already has the member
    REFUSE WHEN the tag cannot be created
    SAYS git tag <name>. The manual: -f replaces an existing tag instead of failing.

ACTION push the branch and the tag
    READS
        the branch
        tags
    CREATE origin's branch FROM the branch
    CREATE origin's tags FROM tags
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
    REFUSE WHEN origin rejects the push
    ACCEPT WHEN origin's tag names the commit pushed
        BECAUSE the ref is already what the push sends, so git takes the push
    REFUSE WHEN origin's tags already has the member
        SAYS An update to a tag origin already has on another commit is rejected without --force.
    SAYS git push --atomic origin <branch> <tag>: both refs are taken, or neither.

ACTION push the branch
    READS the branch
    CREATE origin's branch FROM the branch
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
    REFUSE WHEN origin rejects the push
    SAYS git push origin <branch>.
